<title>UK: Courtaulds Textiles in 1.35 mln stg disposal.</title>
<headline>Courtaulds Textiles in 1.35 mln stg disposal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British textiles group Courtaulds Textiles Plc said on Monday it sold its George Brettle &amp; Co subsidiary to Chilprufe Ltd, a maker of women's underwear, for 1.35 million stg.</p>
<p>Courtaulds said George Brettle, a wholesale supplier of branded womenswear, had net assets of 800,000 stg at the end of last year. Courtaulds said the disposal was part of its programme to focus resources better.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
